.TH PRO-UPDATES 1 "2026-10-09" "pro-updates 1.5.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pro-updates \- list and apply apt and Flatpak updates, with Ubuntu Pro (ESM) status
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pro-updates
.RB [ \-\-check ]
.RB [ \-\-version ]
.RB [ \-\-help ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pro-updates
goes through three sections and asks before each action:
.IP 1. 4
Ubuntu Pro (ESM): universe fixes Canonical publishes only to Ubuntu Pro
subscribers, as reported by the Ubuntu Pro client, with any free remedy (a
Flathub build, or a newer version in another configured repository). Without
the Ubuntu Pro client this section says "not checked".
.IP 2. 4
Flatpak: updates for the Flatpak apps already installed.
.IP 3. 4
Regular apt: the normal apt upgrade. Held packages are never upgraded; updates
that need packages added or removed are named and left alone.
.PP
apt waits up to five minutes for a running update, keeps changed config files,
and never removes a package (\-\-no\-remove), with one exception: after a
Flathub VLC install it offers to remove the VLC .debs, and apt shows the list
and asks. Run it as your normal user; it uses sudo when it needs root, and
exits with 1 when a step failed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-check
Audit only: change nothing. It still reads the network (DNS, and Flathub if a
remote is configured).
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/pro-updates/config.ini
[policy] allow_plaintext = yes|no (default no: updates from plain-http sources
are skipped). Shared with the window.
.TP
.I /etc/pro-updates/pinned\fR, \fI~/.config/pro-updates/pinned
Package names never offered for a Flathub swap, one per line.
.TP
.I /var/lib/pro-updates/holds
Holds made with the window's "Hold back".
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pro-updates-gui (1),
.BR apt-get (8),
.BR flatpak (1)
